        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            An elongated paddle is not a better paddle, it is a different trade. It spends the 24-inch size allowance on reach and leverage, and pays for it with a narrower face and a heavier feel at the net. That trade makes sense for singles players, aggressive drivers and two-handed backhands, and it rarely makes sense for beginners or soft-game doubles players.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you are unsure, start with a standard or hybrid shape, play enough to learn your game, and try an elongated paddle before you buy one. Then use our best pickleball paddles roundup to compare models of the shape that suits you.
          </p>
